WEBVTT

NOTE English translation; original display timings, not word alignment.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.267
Why is there a giraffe
on Zheng He's voyage map?

2
00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:06.367
Open Aden's entry.
There's a curious detail:

3
00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:10.367
Among the king's gifts
to the Ming emperor was a giraffe.

4
00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:13.167
This open-source project is
The World We Know.

5
00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:17.400
Move through the years to see
how much of the world people knew.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.667
Here's the interesting part:

7
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:23.933
Switch perspectives: China or Europe.
Same year, different map fog.

8
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:28.133
A fleet reaching a place doesn't mean
the news has made it back.

9
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.633
The project records
these two times separately.

10
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:34.767
Each little cell stores what was known
from different perspectives.

11
00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.500
As you explore, ask one more question:

12
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.467
Who knew about this place back then?

13
00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:43.400
The map and repository links
are in the comments.
